1
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:41,000
Demek baş be, silav û rêz temaşevanên me yê hêja,
temaşevanên me yê delal.
 
Have a good time. Greetings and respects, our dear viewers,
our precious viewers.

2
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Îro bi xelekeke nû ji bernameya Gundên Welat, ez Rûliyan Hac
Ehmed im.
 
Today, with a new episode of the program Villages of the
Country, I am Ruliyan Haj Ahmed.

3
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:49,000
Û îro me berê xwe daye navçeya gundewarên Raco,
 
And today we have headed to the countryside district of
Rajo,

4
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:53,000
û bi taybet gundê jê re dibêjin Çeqmaqa.
 
and specifically the village called Chaqmaqa.

5
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:57,000
Em ê niha bi hev re biçin seredana gund bikin, derbasî vî
gundî xweşik bibin.
 
We will now go visit the village together, and enter this
beautiful village.

6
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:01,000
Xelkê gund nas bikin, dîroka gund nas bikin û pêşkeşî we
bikin.
 
We will get to know the people of the village, learn the
history of the village, and present it to you.

7
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:21,000
Bi me re bimînin û li me temaşe bikin.
 
Stay with us and watch us.

8
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:43,000
Belê temaşevanên me yê hêja.
 
Yes, our dear viewers.

9
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:45,000
Niha em di navenda gundê Çeqmaqa de ne.
 
We are now in the center of the village of Chaqmaqa.

10
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:48,000
Em hatin vê derê saheke li vê derê heye û darek heye.
 
We came here, there is a square here and a tree.

11
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:51,000
Xelkê gund xwestin me bi vî awayî îstîqbal bikin.
 
The people of the village wanted to welcome us this way.

12
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:55,000
Li vê derê muxtarê gund, kesên bi temen mezin li vê derê
rûniştine.
 
Here, the mukhtar of the village and the elders are sitting
here.

13
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:00,000
Û niha, kesekî bi temen mezin bi me re heye, em ê wî nas
bikin û ew ê dîroka gund ji me re şîrove bike.
 
And now, we have an elderly person with us, we will get to
know him and he will explain the history of the village to
us.

14
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:01,000
Merheba xalo.
 
Hello, uncle.

15
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:02,000
Ehlen we sehlen.
 
Welcome.

16
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:04,000
Em te nas bikin, navê te?
 
Can we get to know you? Your name?

17
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:08,000
Navê min Ehmed Hisên.
 
My name is Ahmed Hussein.

18
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:08,000
Malbata min, malbata...
 
Yes.

19
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:10,000
Malbata min, malbata...
 
My family, the family of...

20
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:11,000
Ser çava.
 
You are welcome.

21
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:12,000
El-Îdrîs.
 
Al-Idris.

22
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:14,000
Belê ser çava.
 
Yes, you are welcome.

23
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:15,000
Ser çavê min.
 
You are welcome.

24
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:21,000
Em dixwazin, tu ji me re hinekî behsa dîroka gundê xwe bikî.
Destpêkê, navê Çeqmaqa ji kû derê hatiye?
 
We want you to tell us a bit about the history of your
village. First, where does the name Chaqmaqa come from?

25
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:26,000
Navê Çeqmaqa, teb'en berê li vê derê Deşta Cûqêmê hebûye.
 
The name Chaqmaqa, naturally, there used to be the Juqem
Plain here.

26
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:30,000
Deşta Cûqêmê gund xirab bûye, hatine,
 
At the Juqem Plain, the village was ruined, they came,

27
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:34,000
şerqî gund heye gundê Zênê, li wir rûniştin.
 
east of the village is Zene village, they settled there.

28
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:38,000
Paşê malbat hatin li vê derê şên kirin.
 
Then families came and settled here.

29
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:40,000
Û nav lê kirin Çeqmaqa.
 
And they named it Chaqmaqa.

30
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:43,000
Çima navê Çeqmaqa, ji kû derê hatiye? Çi manesiya wê heye?
 
Why does the name Chaqmaqa come from there? What is its
meaning?

31
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:46,000
Welle, manesek da wî warî...
 
Well, a meaning to it... this place...

32
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:50,000
Bi deqîq nikarim, bi tehdîd kî... nikarim ji te re bêjim.
 
I can't be precise, I can't exactly specify... I can't tell
you.

33
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:57,000
Nav lê kirin Çeqmaq... Çeqmaqê Mezin. Hîn me zeraîtdarekî
heye Çeqmaqê Çûçik jî heye li vir,
 
They named it Chaqmaq... Big Chaqmaq. We also have a smaller
one, Little Chaqmaq is here too,

34
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:02,000
hatin li vir şên kirin û ew devera wî zemanî hatin çandin,
 
they came and settled here, and around that time they
started planting,

35
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:04,000
yanî...
 
I mean...

36
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:06,000
Di kîjan salê de gundê Çeqmaqa ava bû? We çêkir?
 
In what year was the village of Chaqmaqa established? You
built it?

37
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:10,000
Berî me sed sal, hekî bibêjim... pir li me jor e...
 
A hundred years before us, if I say so... it's much older
than us...

38
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:12,000
Yanî berî sed sal e, sê sed sal e, çar sed sal e...
 
You mean a hundred years ago, three hundred years ago, four
hundred years ago...

39
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:14,000
Ev sê sed sal, zêdetir heye.
 
It's been three hundred years, even more.

40
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:15,000
Belê.
 
Yes.

41
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:16,000
Sê sed sal zêdetir heye.
 
It's been more than three hundred years.

42
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:20,000
Destpêkê yanî gund li vê derê bû lê li jêr bû we anî vê
derê?
 
In the beginning, was the village here or was it lower down
and you brought it here?

43
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:23,000
Ê, anîn vê derê... gund anîn vê derê.
 
Uh, they brought it here... they brought the village here.

44
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:24,000
Belê.
 
Yes.

45
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:27,000
Me gund li vê derê Deşta Cûqêmê heye.
 
We had the village down there in the Juqem Plain.

46
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:32,000
Hatin li vir û jê re digotin Gundê Zênê. Li vê derê, şerqî
gund...
 
They came here and they were called Zene Village. Right
here, east of the village...

47
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:36,000
Û ew jî hatin vê derê şên kirin, di vir de rûniştin.
 
And they also came and settled here, they resided here.

48
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:39,000
Feqet... li vê derê gund mezin bûye.
 
Then... the village grew larger here.

49
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:43,000
Xalo min, ez dixwazim destpêkê zane bim navê Çeqmaqa ji kû
derê hatiye? Navê gundê we...
 
Uncle, I want to know first where the name Chaqmaqa comes
from? The name of your village...

50
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:49,000
Navê Çeqmaqa, tiştê hatîye, li Cûqêmê bû, berê Deşta Cûqêmê
digotin.
 
The name Chaqmaqa, what happened, I was at Juqem, they used
to call it the Juqem Plain.

51
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:55,000
Cami hîn li wir e... diçûn li wir nimêj dikirin. Cihê camiyê
li wir gund xirab bû.
 
The mosque is still there... they would go there and pray.
Instead of the mosque, the village was ruined there.

52
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:58,000
Hatin vê derê, gundê Zênê çêkirin.
 
They came here and built Zene village.

53
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:00,000
Li gundê Zênê jî hatin, vê derê...
 
From Zene village too, they came here...

54
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:02,000
Niha te qala kevirek kir... gazina xwe jê kir...
 
You just mentioned a stone... you talked about it...

55
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:07,000
Kevirê Çeqmaqê, ku şerar dida û pê agir pê dixistin.
 
It's the flintstone (Chaqmaq stone), which gave off sparks
and they would start a fire with it.

56
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:08,000
Belê.
 
Yes.

57
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:13,000
Ser wî yekê... bi pûşekî, agirê pûşekî çêdikirin... Digotin
kevirê Çeqmaqê.
 
On that note... with some dry grass, they would make a fire
with grass... They called it the Chaqmaq stone.

58
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:16,000
Bi kevirê Çeqmaqî, gund li vir çêkirin û wî navî lê kirin.
 
With the Chaqmaq stone, they built the village here and gave
it that name.

59
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:20,000
Yanî em bêjin li ser navê vî kevirî, we nav li gund kir.
 
So we can say you named the village after this stone.

60
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:22,000
Erê, belê.
 
Yes, exactly.

61
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:28,000
Tu dikarî ji me re qala malbatan destpêkê bikî, kî hatin
gundê we? Yên destpêkê hatin gund, kî bûn?
 
Can you tell us about the families in the beginning, who
came to your village? Who were the first to come to the
village?

62
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:32,000
Yên destpêkê... berî kê... du malbat hatin.
 
The first ones... before anyone... two families came.

63
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:38,000
Yek mala Teşî bû, yek mala Kelê bûn.
 
One was the Tashi family, one was the Kale family.

64
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:39,000
Evana... esasiyê gund in.
 
These... are the foundation of the village.

65
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:45,000
Û paşê jî em giş hatin. Niha malbatên we, nako...
 
And then we all came. Now your families, currently...

66
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:47,000
Çiqas e hejmara malbatên gund bi giştî?
 
What is the total number of families in the village?

67
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:54,000
Bi giştî ededê gund heye sê hezar û du sed şexs.
 
In total, the population of the village is three thousand
two hundred people.

68
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:56,000
Û çiqas xanî li gund hene?
 
And how many houses are there in the village?

69
00:04:56,000 --> 00:05:00,000
Sê sed xanî hene nako, belê.
 
There are three hundred houses currently, yes.

70
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:01,000
Sê sed xanî...
 
Three hundred houses...

71
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:03,000
Emm.
 
Mmhmm.

72
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:07,000
Ger em bêjin gundê Çeqmaqa, gundê Çeqmaqa bi çi navdar e?
 
If we say the village of Chaqmaqa, what is the village of
Chaqmaqa famous for?

73
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:12,000
Dema ku dibêjin Çeqmaqa, tiştê yekemîn tê bîra te çiye? Ewa
tê bîra te...
 
When they say Chaqmaqa, what is the first thing that comes
to your mind?

74
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:16,000
Tiştê tê bîra min, ev gundê me, xelk fuqare bûye.
 
The thing that comes to my mind is that our village, the
people used to be poor.

75
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:25,000
Wî zemanî Heleb nedidîtin. Nediçûn. Bi dewêr diçûn, bi hespa
diçûn, bi qatira diçûn.
 
At that time, they didn't see Aleppo. They didn't go. They
went by livestock, by horses, by mules.

76
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:33,000
Diçûn, hew jî li ser çi di'êşan? Di'êşan manê dar û ber a...
û karkerî. Bi wê di'êşan.
 
They would go, and what did they struggle for? They
struggled for trees and stones... and labor. That's what
they struggled with.

77
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:37,000
Yanî li ser komirê bû. Li ser wî tiştî bû. Çopir bû...
 
I mean, it was about coal. It was about that. It was
scavengers...

78
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:40,000
Vêca di vê cîhê de bûn.
 
So they were in this place.

79
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:44,000
Û ziraet paşê dest pê bû. Ziraat derket.
 
And agriculture started later. Agriculture emerged.

80
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:49,000
Ziraat di vir de dest pê bû. Roj bi roj zêdetir bû. Meh bi
meh û sal bi sal zêdetir bû.
 
Agriculture started here. Day by day it increased. Month by
month and year by year it increased.

81
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:53,000
Paşê niha hew tiştên hilhatî li ser ziraetê ne.
 
Then now, the things that have emerged are based on
agriculture.

82
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:58,000
Cihên dîrokî li gundê we... tiştên dîrokî, kevnar hene?
 
Historical places in your village... are there historical,
ancient things?

83
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:01,000
Wekî bibêjim... li muhîtê Çeqmaqê çar kel dixûyîne.
 
As I would say... in the surroundings of Chaqmaqa, four
castles are visible.

84
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:01,000
Kel, kela qedîm.
 
What are they?

85
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:02,000
Kel, kela qedîm.
 
Castles, Ancient Castles.

86
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:03,000
E.
 
Yes.

87
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:05,000
Çar kel dixûyîne muhîtê Çeqmaqê.
 
Four castles are visible in the surroundings of Chaqmaqa.

88
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:07,000
Yanî keleh di gund da heye?
 
You mean there is a castle in the village?

89
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:08,000
Na, di gund da nîne.
 
No, there isn't one in the village.

90
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:11,000
Bes di muhîtê gund da, çar qele hene.
 
But in the surroundings of the village, there are four
castles.

91
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:13,000
Çawan e, min baş fêm nekir...
 
How so, I didn't understand well...

92
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:17,000
Kel li vê derê, Kelûşkê jê re dibêjin.
 
A castle here, they call it Kelushke.

93
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:22,000
Kela gundê Bilîko heye. Û li vê derê heye, keleha rû... li
xerbiya gund.
 
There is the castle of Biliko village. And there is one
here, the castle of the face... in the west of the village.

94
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:24,000
Û çiyayê Bilîl heye, qelek li wir e.
 
And there is Bilil mountain, there is a castle there.

95
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:26,000
A, yanî gundê Çeqmaqa di ortê de ye.
 
Ah, so the village of Chaqmaqa is in the middle.

96
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:29,000
Di ortê de, di muhîtê, çar qele de ye... Belê.
 
It is in the middle, in the surroundings of four castles...
Yes.

97
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:31,000
Û di gund da çi heye? Em bêjin cîhekî dîrokî.
 
And what is in the village? Let's say a historical place.

98
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:32,000
Di gund da, tiştî aserî da...
 
In the village, ancient things...

99
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:36,000
Em bêjin mesela... malên kevin, xaniyên kevin, çi mane jê?
 
Let's say for example... old houses, old buildings, what
remains of them?

100
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:40,000
Xaniyên kevin nemane. Gişt xaniyên nû ko beton in. Yên berê
ax bûne.
 
There are no old houses remaining. All the new houses are
concrete. The old ones were made of mud.

101
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:46,000
Û gişt... avakirina... mafê wan dar û ber in. Moş, kevir,
ba.
 
And all... the buildings... their materials were trees and
stones. Beams, stones, wind.

102
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:48,000
Tiştê girîngiya wî devera ye.
 
The important thing of that region.

103
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:53,000
Yanî evana kiribûn... wî devera, paşê ev gund gişt wî rengî
avabû.
 
I mean, they had done this... that region, then this village
was all built in that manner.

104
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:54,000
Spasiya te dikim, saeta te xweş.
 
I thank you, have a good time.

105
00:06:54,000 --> 00:07:14,000
Ehlen we sehlen.
 
Welcome.

106
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:55,000
Belê temaşevanên me yê hêja.
 
Yes, our dear viewers.

107
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:58,000
Niha jî muxtarê gundê Çeqmaqa bi me re ye.
 
Now, the mukhtar of the village of Chaqmaqa is with us.

108
00:07:58,000 --> 00:08:00,000
Wê ji me re behsa xwendewanên gund bike,
 
He will talk to us about the students of the village,

109
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:04,000
çawa bû xwendin, dibistan kîjan salê de hate avakirin.
 
how was the education, in what year the school was built.

110
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:06,000
Merheba muxtar, em te nas bikin?
 
Hello mukhtar, can we get to know you?

111
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:07,000
Ehlen we sehlen.
 
Welcome.

112
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:14,000
Navê min... Birîm e. Ji gundê Çeqmaqa me.
 
My name is... Birim. I am from the village of Chaqmaqa.

113
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:18,000
Tu bi intixabata ketiye, an demoqratî... bixwe...
 
You came in by elections, or democratic... right...

114
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:21,000
Teyîn... ne demoqratî ye û ne jî teyîn e.
 
Appointed... it is neither democratic nor appointed.

115
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:24,000
Em bi hevdu re amade ne, bibim eger na ez muxtar im.
 
We are ready together, to become one if not I am the
mukhtar.

116
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:27,000
Muxtar bixwe eger navek lê bikim,
 
The mukhtar himself, if I give him a name,

117
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:29,000
xizmetkar e.
 
he is a servant.

118
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:33,000
Em di xizmeta gundê xwe de bin, em di xizmeta miletê xwe de
bin.
 
We are in the service of our village, we are in the service
of our nation.

119
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:39,000
Ev qafî ye, yanî ne em muxtar xelkê ser miletê xwe, ser
gundê xwe, xwe bibînin.
 
This is sufficient, meaning we don't see ourselves as
mukhtar lords over our people, over our village.

120
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:41,000
Em wisa temam dikin.
 
We complete it like this.

121
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:45,000
Ser serê me, Xwedê ji te razî be.
 
On our heads, may God be pleased with you.

122
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:49,000
Belê, niha em dikarin hinekî biçin zemanê berê.
 
Yes, now can we somewhat go back to the old times.

123
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:54,000
Xwendewan wek ez dizanim, di gundê we de gelekî pirr in.
 
Students, as I know, are very numerous in your village.

124
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:56,000
Ez dixwazim bizanibim, destpêkê xwendin li cem we çawa bû?
 
I want to know, how was the education with you in the
beginning?

125
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:59,000
Û kîjan salê de dibistan ava bû?
 
And in what year was the school built?

126
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:04,000
Di destpêkê de, berê li cem xoca dixwendin.
 
In the beginning, they used to study with the hodja
(teacher).

127
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:07,000
Berî li cem xoca dixwendin...
 
Before, they used to study with the hodja...

128
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:14,000
Li vê derê mamosteyek hebe, digotin Mihemed Hebeş, zaroka
xwendin dida.
 
There was a teacher here, they called him Mihemed Hebesh, he
used to teach the children.

129
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:16,000
Carê xwendin didan.
 
Sometimes they gave lessons.

130
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:24,000
Û di dera mamoste Ehmed Şêxo, Ehmed Dawid ew jî diçûn li bin
dara xwendin didan.
 
And around that time teachers Ahmed Shexo, Ahmed Dawid, they
also went and taught under the trees.

131
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:29,000
Dû re, piştî vê emrê zehf, mekteb hat ava kirin.
 
Later, after a long time, a school was built.

132
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:30,000
Dibistan hat ava kirin.
 
A school was built.

133
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:37,000
Va dibistana Çeqmaqa, hatiye avakirin di sala 1956'an de.
 
This school of Chaqmaqa was built in the year 1956.

134
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:39,000
Da em kurt bikin,
 
Let's keep it short,

135
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:47,000
berî 1956'an da, dibistan li gundê we tunebûye, li ber xoca
dixwendin. Mamoste di bin darê da elimandin.
 
before 1956, there was no school in your village, they
studied with the Hodja. Teachers taught under the tree.

136
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:49,000
Erê weha bû.
 
Yes, it was like that.

137
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:51,000
Li ber xoca bû, li ber mela bû.
 
It was with the hodja, it was with the mullah.

138
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:53,000
Li ber şêxa bû.
 
It was with the sheikhs.

139
00:09:53,000 --> 00:10:00,000
Xwendina cizû e'mmê bû, xwendina quranê bû, bes ji pey pêncî
û şeşan de...
 
It was studying the Juz' Amma, it was studying the Quran,
but after fifty-six...

140
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:04,000
...pêş ketiye bi pêş ketiye, bi zanebûnê bi pêş ketiye.
 
...has advanced, has advanced, has advanced with knowledge.

141
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:11,000
Yanî belê xwendin e, elm e, zanebûn e, te kê miletî ku
bikuje, herve nakuje.
 
I mean yes, it is reading, it is science, it is knowledge,
if you want to kill a nation, it doesn't kill just like
that.

142
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:18,000
Te kê miletî ku pêş xe, qelemê pê de, zanebûnê pê de.
 
If you want to advance a nation, give it a pen, give it
knowledge.

143
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:23,000
Wê çaxê wê çaxê milet pêş de ketiye, milet xwendî ye.
 
At that time, at that time the nation has advanced, the
nation is educated.

144
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:30,000
Cehil pîs e. Dijminê te wî selef, dijminê te wî selef e di
miletan da.
 
Ignorance is bad. Your biggest enemy, your biggest enemy is
among the nations.

145
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:34,000
Cehilbûn, nezanbûn... û gir e.
 
Ignorance, lack of knowledge... and it is heavy.

146
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:40,000
Em dibêjin kesên nexwendin, ger keçik dibe, ger xort dibe.
Çi kar dikirin? Li gund?
 
We say those who did not read, whether a girl or a boy. What
work did they do? In the village?

147
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:48,000
Diçûn şivantiyê dikirin, diçûn cot dajotin, cot dajotin,
şivantiyê dikirin.
 
They went and did shepherding, they went and ploughed,
ploughed, did shepherding.

148
00:10:48,000 --> 00:11:00,000
Diçûn nêçîrê, diçûn êzingan, pê jiber malbata xwe bihecînin,
jiber tiştên xwe... ba dewam dikirin.
 
They went hunting, they went for firewood, so they could
provide for their families, for their things... they
continued.

149
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:04,000
Xalê Muxtar, spasîya te dikim. Saeta te xweş, dîtina te
gelekî xweşîk bû.
 
Uncle Mukhtar, I thank you. May your time be pleasant,
seeing you was very nice.

150
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:24,000
Xwedê ji te razî be.
 
May God be pleased with you.

151
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:08,000
Belê, temaşevanên me yên hêja, niha jî em hatin e malekê, li
navenda gundê Çeqmaqa ye...
 
Yes, our dear viewers, now we have come to a house, in the
center of Çeqmaqa village...

152
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:14,000
Xalê Mustefa bi me re ye. Xalê Mustefa yek ji mirovên li ser
dîrokê, ne dîrokê, gund deng kî...
 
Uncle Mustafa is with us. Uncle Mustafa is one of the people
to talk about history, no not history, the village...

153
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:23,000
Li ser kesên ku hatin e Efrînê, ger Fransa dibe, ger Îngîlîz
dibe, ger tiştên em dibêjin ehdasên tarîxî têde bûne, ew ser
wê mijarê deng e.
 
About the people who came to Afrin, whether it's France,
whether it's the English, whether things we call historical
events happened in it, he is a voice on that subject.

154
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:24,000
Merheba xalo!
 
Hello uncle!

155
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:25,000
Ehlen!
 
Welcome!

156
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:26,000
Em te nas bikin?
 
Let us get to know you?

157
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:32,000
Navê min bilêvkere, Mihemed Hemdê. Ji gundê Çeqmaqê ye.
 
Pronounce my name, Mihemed Hemde. From the village of
Çeqmaq.

158
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:33,000
Çeqmaqa mezin.
 
Big Çeqmaq.

159
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:37,000
Yan Çeqmaqa mezin e.
 
Or it's big Çeqmaq.

160
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:46,000
Deke ji me re ser tiştên kevin deng kî. Em bi ehdasên di vir
da bûne, Fransizan hatin vir, kî hat vir, beriya me hûn haya
we lê hene, emrê te çiqas e xalo?
 
Please tell us about the old things. The events that
happened here, the French came here, who came here, before
us you were aware of it, how old are you uncle?

161
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:50,000
Ez, emrê min e niha 94 e, 94.
 
Me, my age is now 94, 94.

162
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:53,000
Te gihiştîyê, te gihişt Fransa l'viran? Wa dîtin e we?
 
Did you reach them, did you reach France here? Did you see
them?

163
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:53,000
Te gihişt Îngilîzan l'virana?
 
Yes.

164
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:54,000
Te gihişt Îngilîzan l'virana?
 
Did you reach the English here?

165
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:55,000
Erê, gihiştimê.
 
Yes, I reached them.

166
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:57,000
Deki wan ji me re hewal dê?
 
Can you tell us about them?

167
00:12:57,000 --> 00:13:02,000
Min ji te re got ev tişt stûn bû, bes e de ne ez gihiştim e
Fransizan û di nav Îngilîzan...
 
I told you this thing was a pillar, but anyway I reached the
French and among the English...

168
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:12,000
ez gihiştim e adî, û nî gundê ronkir koçê me, gundê ronî li
berê pê va nişbûn, me du xwar di dan espêciyan.
 
I reached them normally, and they brightened the village our
migration, the bright village in the front was settled, we
gave two meals to the horsemen.

169
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:17,000
Osman beg bi, mesulê wan, hat li daştî cîhê niha.
 
It was Osman Beg, their official, he came to the plain place
now.

170
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:31,000
Bê dar me kerta hel da avêt da got e şeş gundî ko bi min de.
Bavkê min ji go be, çi ereban e yanî qedena têda nan.
 
Without trees we took the paper threw it said give me six
villagers. My father also said okay, whatever Arab it is I
mean prohibition in it bread.

171
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:38,000
Şeş çuwal kirin, genim hel da heftê, hel da heftê çû şeş me
re wanî...
 
They made six sacks, took the wheat for seventy, took it for
seventy went six...

172
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:43,000
Taxtik kirin, li dora garanê çû ser wê xetê...
 
They made a board, went around the herd on that line...

173
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:53,000
Got ha va 25 çuwal e kî werin? Got penc çuwal ê Fransizan e
û got bîstan ji te be emir.
 
He said here are 25 sacks who will come? He said five sacks
belong to the French and said twenty will be yours by order.

174
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:59,000
Penc çuwal rahê kirin û birin. Û şeş gundî ko.
 
They loaded five sacks and took them. And six villagers.

175
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:08,000
Çûn mesele ker eskerê di hatin, eskerê di hatin dîrok ve di
nan, dîrokî kar e bê, dîrok..
 
They went to the issue that soldiers were coming, soldiers
were coming they were putting history, historical work,
history..

176
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:10,000
Heval li Efrînê bû? Yan l' gund bû, dema li gund bû?
 
Was the friend in Afrin? Or in the village, when it was in
the village?

177
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:14,000
L' ber l' ber, ba di nan di birin Bilbilê.
 
In the front, in the front, they were putting and taking
them to Bilbil.

178
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:24,000
Rabû hat e ba bavikê min sîxre da, me çû bu Osman beg re
got, anî perê qerax da me, me lê man bavê dirav da kirin û
çûn.
 
He got up and came to my father forced him, we went and told
Osman Beg, he brought and gave us the money of the edge, we
stayed on it the father gave the money and they went.

179
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:33,000
Got em na birin. Em na birin şuxul. Paşê min ew gêndir re
bon. Li dilbir...
 
Said we will not take it. We will not take the work. Later I
was rolling them. At Dilbir...

180
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:38,000
Min re bon daf ser min na gêş tinê.
 
They ran and set a trap on me they did not catch me.

181
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:42,000
Min wanî hat mat, bavikê min bi sibehê got raze me di haka
ber dim rû.
 
I came like this amazed, my father said in the morning sleep
we are putting it like this in front of the face.

182
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:46,000
Bi sibehê me dî xistin çûn. Ha bes tiştk tine, ibad..
 
In the morning we saw they hit and went. Ha but there is
nothing, worship..

183
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:50,000
Te Dîlber xêr ra bon? Te Dîlber xêr ra bon?
 
Did you run away from Dilber? Did you run away from Dilber?

184
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:53,000
Dîlber reyê Osman beg bû.
 
Dilber was the president of Osman Beg.

185
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:55,000
Reîsê Fransa? Pormîş te na dîn.
 
President of France? You did not see Pormish.

186
00:14:55,000 --> 00:15:00,000
Defter min na gêş tî min, pormiş min nebû. Bavkê min ji
got..
 
My notebook did not reach me, I did not have a pormish. My
father also said..

187
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:08,000
Kes isbê di ser nîne.. Bê sibeh ji hat, an çûn kinayî,
Dilbir l'mira mo.
 
No one is on top.. Early morning he came, or went entirely,
Dilbir stayed with me.

188
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:13,000
Em l' ber firkê re bûn e hatin Dilbir, ebwa nasi kirî...
 
We ran from the flight and came to Dilbir, those
acquaintances...

189
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:24,000
Ebo nes mişib rabo got, got minî duyê bo Mhemed Cemor. Got
noka hî bir. Çû Dîlber da dest min çû.. Ha wa çû...
 
... He said my second is for Mihemed Cemor. Said now he took
it. He went and gave Dilber to my hand and went.. That's how
he went...

190
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:35,000
Zan e, wekî desotî bi gundî ji. Ewwelan devê ce... li pêşî
malê teşîr e bilçir e.
 
He knows, like he was burnt with the villager too. Firstly
the mouth of... in front of the house is famous, is bright.

191
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:37,000
Rasî te?
 
Really?

192
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:47,000
Haho, çar bab in a... Paşê gund hatin her hendî darikê ba
hatin gund mezin bî. Gund mezin bî.
 
Haho, these are four fathers... Then the villages came,
every bit of tree came, the village became big. The village
became big.

193
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:55,000
Ha bo çar bab in a.. ev dibêjin a gundîn. Çar bab... ewwel
wehd e... devê ce...
 
Here they are four fathers.. these they say are villagers.
Four fathers... the first one... mouth of...

194
00:15:55,000 --> 00:16:03,000
Pêşî Hemze, li layê gundî, pêşî Hemze navê gundî, bavikê min
di navê gundê me huwiye...
 
First Hemze, on the side of the village, first Hemze name of
the villager, my father in the name of our village...

195
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:11,000
Tac ro me hwî, Hemzû lîno lêxwa. Bema bo, noka çar bab bi
nav libirin.
 
... But for now four fathers took the name.

196
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:17,000
Xalê min, nuha te ser Fransa ji me ra deng kir, tu kanê hekî
ji mara ser Îngilîzan deng kî?
 
My uncle, now you talked to us about France, can you talk to
us about the English?

197
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:20,000
Û te çend salê bî dema Îngilîz hatin?
 
And how old were you when the English came?

198
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:23,000
Îngilîz ez fehm dikim bi mortox.
 
The English I understand with mortox.

199
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:30,000
Daxî îngilîz hatî qeçi çun şixul în, kincî xwa di vi ra qit
bin... Me jina ewir bişunda na...
 
When the English came, kids went to work, their clothes were
short from here... We women did not...

200
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:36,000
Çima we jina nadî? Jin diçûn ber xwe dirêz dikirin ma lam l'
xwe daştî. Mane sori bi anî...
 
Why didn't you give women? Women went and prolonged
themselves...

201
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:45,000
Mehnê bi qehirmin... Hewna me dît Îngilîz di bera deştê dîn
a, gubar a qayîm bi. Paşê zehf donikê çûn ba dexare bi...
 
Meaning with heroes... There we saw the English in front of
the plain, there was heavy dust. Then very many went...

202
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:50,000
Çu çar tehton ew nîn, kirin e şikê qayfê...
 
...

203
00:16:50,000 --> 00:17:01,000
Taxtê bilad... Heno, û Firansiz l'bê pîs dîn a. Cam erdê bi
mecî dîn a. Er çim ewî Firansiz hatim di çim cem.
 
The board of the country... Then, and the French... I go to
that French I came I go to him.

204
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:04,000
En noxî re ênoq di don me...
 
They give us enoq...

205
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:08,000
Ênab di don me.. di bera pê berzil hatin.
 
They give us enab..

206
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:13,000
Ênop? Enop çiye? En, gelok wa kiya? Ma di xwarin?
 
Enop? What is Enop? En, ...? We ate?

207
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:17,000
Ênab in nabê xon!
 
Enab in the name of eating!

208
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:23,000
Di han, de don espojî.. Meyro ji doxor...
 
... They gave to the horsemen.. Men also ate...

209
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:29,000
Tozan hesbo, merî ji de xwar! Wakî tenik tera... Ha!
 
Dust of horses, people also ate! Like thin... Ha!

210
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:35,000
Me de xwarin. Koçê me tac kir me wanî hat mal. Belê!
 
We ate. Our migration was crowned we came home like this.
Yes!

211
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:38,000
Çiqas sal Îngilîz li vir ma? Tê bîr a te?
 
How many years did the English stay here? Do you remember?

212
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:41,000
Welleh nikanim, nêzîkî penc sal a ba.
 
By God I can't, it was close to five years.

213
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:44,000
Hawa ti kîjan salê de bî tê bîr a te ye?
 
So what year were you in do you remember?

214
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:48,000
Sal a ez nizanim. Sala xwe ez nizanim. Xwendiniya me tîne!
 
The year I don't know. My year I don't know. We don't have
reading (education)!

215
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:52,000
Ne wa bi mekî... Niha kanê Îngilîz bera kî ho, lê Firansa
bera kî hot?
 
Not that... Now who did the English send, but who did France
send?

216
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:54,000
Firansa ba Îngilîz ket der.
 
France got out with the English.

217
00:17:54,000 --> 00:18:02,000
He wî çaxî tû çûçik bî? Ee, ket ba derê paşî bera pir k'çî
xwa yo hîş kir bîn asker.
 
At that time you were a kid? Yes, fell out later ...

218
00:18:02,000 --> 00:18:09,000
L'bê gundî ji çûn de da, a ni xîri xwandînî min tîne. De
bobkê me san dim bar pês.
 
... From the village they went, ... I have no reading. ...

219
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:14,000
Paşê çûm ew kirin.. teko co ereb çêbûn ez rabûm çûm ho ker
eskerî..
 
Then I went they did that.. when Arabs were formed I got up
went to do military..

220
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:18,000
pênc şeş ro cêl worm om.. qenê terê.
 
five six days ...

221
00:18:18,000 --> 00:18:24,000
Lê, go ji me re hewal da dema eskerî ta çawa bû? Ksere
eskerî xwe ji me re hewal de...
 
But, tell us how was your military time? Tell us about your
military...

222
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:31,000
Yê eskerî xwa, çûm. Me eskerî îcbarî xelas kir... Tek ra hat
e mal.
 
My military, I went. We finished the compulsory military...
Then came home.

223
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:39,000
Me sekir pere tinen e, me çû l' Efrînê em ze kir em çûm
Heleb. Ji Heleb birin Hama Hums ê derbas kirin.
 
We looked there is no money, we went to Afrin, we went to
Aleppo. From Aleppo they took to Hama Homs they passed.

224
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:44,000
Çûm l'wê derê şeş meh ez ro kirim Siwêda...
 
I went there for six months they put me in Suwayda...

225
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:51,000
Tizne as sêw ê dem o. He çûm ser hepsê... Neme yîmze kir.
 
... I went to the prison... We didn't sign.

226
00:18:51,000 --> 00:19:00,000
Paşî mişkîlek di nav da çêbû.. gotin hen şaşî na hên çina
nizanim, rike me di navî me pêncî mirov der ket.
 
Later a problem happened in the middle.. they said there are
mistakes I don't know, ... fifty people came out.

227
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:08,000
Û hm bum ara wa ma l' wira... em lê xistin hatin îda da ma
na...
 
And ... we hit came ...

228
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:16,000
Paş e ma, li pêncî sal ak şûn da, Cemal Ebdu Nasir ho hukim
kir li ber derê a şî... he çûm.
 
Later remained, fifty years later, Gamal Abdel Nasser ruled
in front of the door ... I went.

229
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:20,000
Xelep ... Wereq mi cur da me, gih ha perê we yîne.
 
Aleppo ... They gave me a paper, here is your money.

230
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:25,000
Tê got qat per, mi hê da wereq me qut e ker mî, Daxa dî,
eskeriya te me şep te de.
 
... He said money, I gave the paper ...

231
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:31,000
E tiş cî didin te pere te ne nê xwa dil bin. Heba l'me xitik
in.
 
... They give you place your money ...

232
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:37,000
Û der perê xwa nî hem midor dez o ba tê tê m'go bo pera na e
kam dikim hê nê.
 
And ...

233
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:42,000
Go te her re ba qir Qahîr e. Kî der e Misr re.
 
He said you go to Cairo. Where to Egypt.

234
00:19:42,000 --> 00:20:00,000
M'go ho ha ra xwîn e nîvê mê nî bê ta, go mawşûr te tê pirs
kirî. M'go de her e...
 
I said ... He said ... I said go ...

235
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:10,000
Ê ew jê dîyekî di dused waraqî da, go yabo ko her xelas e.
Go banq Elqahîre, wira... go herin perê xwe ji wê werin.
 
He gave me a two hundred lira bill and said, "Dad, just go,
it's finished." He said, "Come to Banque du Caire." He said,
"Go get your money from there."

236
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:13,000
Dige şixul te ba kanî ke te robaş xwend da Misrî?
 
Did your work go well that you got a good return in Egypt?

237
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:15,000
Na ew yek gavê tu Şamê ne Misir î.
 
No, at that time you were in Damascus, not Egypt.

238
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:18,000
Ê.. giş xirap te be kanî tişt?
 
Yeah.. did it all go bad for you?

239
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:23,000
Ew de kê me bikenî min dema cab daye, min got kê me bikene.
 
If they wanted to mock me, I would immediately answer, I
said who is going to mock me.

240
00:20:23,000 --> 00:20:30,000
Hema de go, go her xelas e... Banq Elqahîre go li wê derê
ye... go herin perê xwe wî ra werin.
 
He just said, go, it's finished... Banque du Caire, he said
it's over there... he said go get your money from him.

241
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:31,000
Belê.
 
Yes.

242
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:36,000
Min wekî çûm wê derê, go eskerê li wê derê... go komyosyon ê
çer e.
 
When I went there, he said the soldier is over there... he
said the commission is whatever.

243
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:41,000
Çûm eskerê li wê derê sîlah bi dest e.. Selam aleykum, go
aleykum selam.
 
I went to the soldier there, a weapon in his hand.. Peace be
upon you, he said and upon you be peace.

244
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:44,000
Min weraq da destê, go her îçê.
 
I handed him the paper, he said go inside.

245
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:50,000
Çûm îçê.. maşelleh tişt... wekî te, eva ciwan a.. belkî
bîstan a.
 
I went inside... wow things... like you, these youths..
maybe twenty of them.

246
00:20:50,000 --> 00:20:56,000
Min da destê yekî go her wira.. çûm wira go her wira.. çûm
wira go her wê derê. Çûm...
 
I gave it to one, he said go there.. I went there he said go
there.. I went there he said go over there. I went...

247
00:20:56,000 --> 00:21:03,000
Paşê derek dîtim go her perê xwe ba wer.. Min perê xwe
anîn.. Ew çar sed û deh weraq..
 
Then I found a door, he said go bring your money.. I brought
my money.. It was four hundred and ten liras..

248
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:08,000
Çar sed û deh weraq dan min.. Min wextê hewşek kirrî, bi sed
û pêncî weraqî.
 
They gave me four hundred and ten liras.. At that time I
