363
00:30:32,000 --> 00:30:33,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

364
00:30:33,000 --> 00:30:38,000
Mîj, ma didane pêşî mîvan ê, helaw. Hejîr wan e zivistanan
e, me karê xwe bît ê, em berhev dikin.
 
Raisins, we would put them in front of the guests, the
sweet. Those are the figs of winter, we do our work and
prepare them.

365
00:30:38,000 --> 00:30:40,000
Xaltî noka hûn çi dikin? Heta noka hûn çi dikin?
 
Auntie, what do you do now? Until now, what do you do?

366
00:30:40,000 --> 00:30:44,000
Heta noka em çi dikin, hejîrê hişk û navê gundê me Qirma ye.
 
What we do until now, dried figs, and the name in our
village is Qirma.

367
00:30:44,000 --> 00:30:45,000
Navê xwe Qirma ye?
 
Its name is Qirma?

368
00:30:45,000 --> 00:30:48,000
Erê, hinek ha ne dibêjin basîq, hinek ha ne dibêjin qirma.
 
Yes, some call it basîq, some call it qirma.

369
00:30:48,000 --> 00:30:51,000
Na ez zanim basîq... hejîrê hişk başqe ye, basîq başqe ye?
 
No, I know basîq... are dried figs different, and is basîq
different?

370
00:30:51,000 --> 00:30:58,000
Hejîr ê hişk başqa ye, ha wa hejîrê hişk başqa ye, em
radixin, û basîq başqa ye.
 
Dried figs are different, yes, dried figs are different, we
lay them out, and basîq is different.

371
00:30:58,000 --> 00:31:00,000
Na basîq ez zanim ê tirî e, yê hejîran heye?
 
No, I know basîq is from grapes, are there fig ones?

372
00:31:00,000 --> 00:31:02,000
Em yê tiriyan çêdikin.
 
We make the grape ones.

373
00:31:02,000 --> 00:31:03,000
Ê tiriyan.
 
The grape ones.

374
00:31:03,000 --> 00:31:04,000
Li cem hewa dereca wa tirî heye?
 
Are there grapes near you in your area?

375
00:31:04,000 --> 00:31:07,000
Erê, tirî heye.
 
Yes, there are grapes.

376
00:31:07,000 --> 00:31:10,000
We noka wek muhaded tirê te xwastiye, yan aw e, kîjan nabin?
 
Do you have a specific kind of grape you need, or are they
all fine, which ones are not fine?

377
00:31:10,000 --> 00:31:17,000
Na ew aw e, bes ê reş nabe ê reş, ê zer e ma wekî şerbetê
xwakî paq be, e binî ye pak bibe.
 
No, they are all fine, but the black ones don't work, the
black ones. The yellow ones work. The juice must be clean,
the bottom must be clean.

378
00:31:17,000 --> 00:31:26,000
Em çêbikin, em e wê şerbetê pak bikelînin, di quzikê kin, û
simîtê xwe hî me hûrî ye, e me nav kin, em ê bu ser sîniya
kin û qut kin.
 
We make it, we boil the juice cleanly, we put it in a pot,
and we put the fine simît (bulgur) in it, we put it on a
tray and cut it.

379
00:31:26,000 --> 00:31:29,000
Xaltîk te behsê aw a kir, me dîsî te behsê cil.
 
Auntie, you mentioned this, we also heard you mention the
"cil" (carpet/rug).

380
00:31:29,000 --> 00:31:34,000
Cil ji li hundira ra çêdikin, cilî ji li hundir re çêdikin,
cilî li hundira çêdikin e mûrî çêdikin.
 
They make the "cil" inside. They make the "cil" inside, they
make the threads inside.

381
00:31:34,000 --> 00:31:42,000
Serbetan a berê tune bûn, dekim me çêdikir, mîvanek me bota,
me çêdikirin ser. Haw a yanê...
 
There were no blankets in the past. We used to make them, if
a guest came to us, we would put them on top. Like this, you
know...

382
00:31:42,000 --> 00:31:43,000
Û haw e çawa çêdikirin?
 
And how did they make this?

383
00:31:43,000 --> 00:31:50,000
Haw a jî dirêstin, bi teşe ha bû, teşe ba ristana e guluk
dikirina me e zerka kir, e tabane çêkir a.
 
They used to spin it, with a spindle, they would take the
spindle and make it into a ball, they would spin it, make
the base.

384
00:31:50,000 --> 00:31:57,000
Çêkirin, çêkirin navî hebû, tiştek e kerkît a we ra dibin, e
ser wî nişta cil e çêkir, cil çêkir xelas kir.
 
They made it, made it, it had a name. There was a thing
called a comb (kerkît), they would sit on it and make the
rug, they would finish making the rug.

385
00:31:57,000 --> 00:32:05,000
Me wekî qut kir me dî kû cilkî me re çêbî, xweş bûye.
 
We would cut it, we would see that a nice rug was made for
us.

386
00:32:05,000 --> 00:32:11,000
Û paşê î lîfê çêdikirin, haw a jî me hêliya hundir dikin.
Haw wa jî hundir a.
 
And then they would make the loofahs, we would spin those
inside too. That is inside too.

387
00:32:11,000 --> 00:32:12,000
Haw wa giş destê jinan da çêdibin?
 
Were all of these made by the women's hands?

388
00:32:12,000 --> 00:32:14,000
Haw wa destê jinan çêdibin.
 
These were all made by women's hands.

389
00:32:14,000 --> 00:32:15,000
Xaltî te ne çetin bûn?
 
Auntie, wasn't it difficult?

390
00:32:15,000 --> 00:32:19,000
Çetin bûn. Rext bûn diçûn ê av ê ji bîrê tînan, bi keran a.
 
It was difficult. In the past, they would go and fetch water
from the well with donkeys.

391
00:32:19,000 --> 00:32:24,000
Av ê li bîrê bi anîna, nan e çêkirana. Û paşê teşîyê xwe
diristin a.
 
They would bring the water from the well, they would make
the bread. And then they would spin their spindle.

392
00:32:24,000 --> 00:32:30,000
Hîn dewî xwe jî bi aw a dikutin, bi fîşek ha bû. Bi fîşek ek
dikutin, rûn jê derxistin o.
 
They would also pound their buttermilk with water, with a
churn. They would pound it with a churn, extract the butter
from it.

393
00:32:30,000 --> 00:32:40,000
Paşê teşê xwe deristana e, me'niya çi? Me'niye wekî jinên
berê, ne mîna yên naha ne, rûneniştar we rehet e.
 
Then they would spin their wool, what I mean is, I mean...
back then women didn't rest like they do now, they didn't
have time to sit comfortably.

394
00:32:40,000 --> 00:32:44,000
Tim kar dikir, heta êvare.
 
They would always work, until the evening.

395
00:32:44,000 --> 00:32:47,000
Naha pirsek me heye, xaltî.
 
Now I have a question, auntie.

396
00:32:47,000 --> 00:32:48,000
Bêje,
 
Tell me.

397
00:32:48,000 --> 00:32:50,000
Wa makyaj dikirin?
 
Did they wear makeup?

398
00:32:50,000 --> 00:32:58,000
Kêm, kêm. Bêre da wekî... nika min dît wekê çêkir, wek kêm
çûnûdi çêkiriye, ez dixwazim vî tiştî bizanibim.
 
A little, a little. Back then... Now I saw how she did it,
she put on a little bit of makeup, I wanted to know about
this thing.

399
00:32:58,000 --> 00:33:00,000
Me qelem hebû makiyajê çavan, hişîn hebû?
 
Did you have an eye pencil, was there blue makeup?

400
00:33:00,000 --> 00:33:10,000
Na qet xebere wa nîn, hişîn nedidin, hêmre te dît ê axa we
başqatir û çav reş kirin hebû.
 
No, there was no such talk, they didn't use blue. There was
red, red was better than that and there was eye blackening.

401
00:33:10,000 --> 00:33:12,000
Hawa... dekim e ma çi dikir.
 
So what did they do.

402
00:33:12,000 --> 00:33:12,000
Dekim me çidikr, tiştek wekî rayîjo ye, çi çêdikir, e sîlekê
dikalin ba.
 
What did they do?

403
00:33:12,000 --> 00:33:17,000
Dekim me çidikr, tiştek wekî rayîjo ye, çi çêdikir, e sîlekê
dikalin ba.
 
What we did, we put something, like a root, they would put
it on a hot plate.

404
00:33:17,000 --> 00:33:24,000
Ê zeyte di çanikekê da kir o, paçek di wê zeytê da bela,
fîtîle fît dikir.
 
They would put oil in a bowl, they would wrap a piece of
cloth around it, making it like a wick.

405
00:33:24,000 --> 00:33:38,000
Dibin sîl ekê kir, da bin tiştekî kir, dû derdikira e dû
derdikiro. Hawa.. ew e dûrê reş dibû reşk dihat.
 
They would put it under the hot plate, they would put it
under something, smoke would come out of it. The smoke would
gather. It would become black.

406
00:33:38,000 --> 00:33:42,000
Navî xwe hêsinek hebû qelem e çavî kîl dida.
 
There was a metal tool for this, they would put it in the
eyes with a pencil.

407
00:33:42,000 --> 00:33:48,000
Hawa jî e çêkirin a hawa reşko, diçûye kuştîyê krî re.
Pêşiye çavê xo pê kil dida.
 
Yes, they made it like that, they made black, they put it in
a box. Then they would put it in their eyes with it.

408
00:33:48,000 --> 00:33:49,000
Qelem tune bû!
 
There was no pencil!

409
00:33:49,000 --> 00:33:56,000
Û sur dikirin li hona? Hemre... hebû hemre qotiyek heye mîna
bulû var û...
 
And they put on lipstick there? There was red... there was a
box of red, like powder...

410
00:33:56,000 --> 00:33:57,000
Te dikir?
 
Did you do it?

411
00:33:57,000 --> 00:34:00,000
Lê min nedikir, ma çeta bizana.
 
No, I didn't do it, how would I know.

412
00:34:00,000 --> 00:34:02,000
Te jê xwe rinta maşallah.
 
But you are very beautiful, mashallah.

413
00:34:02,000 --> 00:34:07,000
Wa da jî xweş, pir xweş, xwedê can beden a we sax be.
 
May your time be beautiful, very beautiful, may God grant
you health.

414
00:34:07,000 --> 00:34:09,000
Canê te, xudê wefe ke nedarê.
 
Bless your soul, may God protect you.

415
00:34:09,000 --> 00:34:29,000
Saet we jî xweş, em pir kêfxweş bîn, înşallah em ê pir hev
dibînin.
 
Good health to you, we were very happy, hopefully we will
see each other often.

416
00:35:15,000 --> 00:35:17,000
Merheba xalo.
 
Hello uncle.

417
00:35:17,000 --> 00:35:18,000
Ehlen wesahlen.
 
Welcome.

418
00:35:18,000 --> 00:35:19,000
Navê te em nas bikin?
 
Can we get to know your name?

419
00:35:19,000 --> 00:35:22,000
Ez Xelîl Husên, gundê Çeqmaqa.
 
I am Xelîl Husên, from the village of Çeqmaqa.

420
00:35:22,000 --> 00:35:31,000
Noka wek em zanin, ku li herêmê Efrîn ê bi giştî, gundê me
da bi taybetî, gelek zor û zehmetî di avê da dikişînin.
 
Now, as we know, in the Afrin region in general, and in our
village in particular, they suffer a lot of hardship and
difficulty regarding water.

421
00:35:31,000 --> 00:35:38,000
Ku cafav çêbû ye nizam çi çêbû ye û gelek tişt. Em kewine
ser gundê we, av çawa ye noka em bêjin li gund?
 
Since the drought happened, I don't know what happened and
many things. We are talking about your village, how is the
water now in the village?

422
00:35:38,000 --> 00:35:46,000
Welleh gundê me ye ji berê û heta niha, tim em avê me tune
ye. Ji zû va.
 
By God, our village, from the past until now, we always have
a lack of water. Since a long time ago.

423
00:35:46,000 --> 00:35:52,000
Bi şev da radibûn diçûn ser bîrê, heta av ji me re dihanî.
 
At night they used to get up and go to the well, to bring us
water.

424
00:35:52,000 --> 00:35:58,000
Av jî îstîhlaka wê berê kêm bû ne wekî niha bû.
 
The consumption of water was low in the past, not like it is
now.

425
00:35:58,000 --> 00:36:03,000
Niha îstîhlaka avê pir e. Henefî çêbûne û şûştin zêde
çêbûye.
 
Now the consumption of water is high. Faucets have been
installed and washing has increased.

426
00:36:03,000 --> 00:36:12,000
Însan yanî zêde îhtîmam dike bi xwe, fe av zêde derre, fe
zehmetiya avê gelek e.
 
People, I mean, care more about themselves, so more water is
consumed, so the difficulty with water is great.

427
00:36:12,000 --> 00:36:13,000
Ava xwe hûn ji kû tînin?
 
Where do you bring your water from?

428
00:36:13,000 --> 00:36:18,000
Em dikirin welle. Em bi seharîca tînin. Seharîc têne ji me
re vala dikin.
 
We buy it, by God. We bring it with water tankers. The water
tankers come and empty it for us.

429
00:36:18,000 --> 00:36:27,000
Xezanên erdê hene, di zivistanê, em çiqas çêbibe, baran
bibare, yanî çiqas musaide bike.
 
There are underground tanks, in the winter, as much as
possible, if it rains, I mean, as much as it allows.

430
00:36:27,000 --> 00:36:33,000
Wê baranê em mehefeze dikin, heta xelas bibe. Xelas bibe şûn
da em bi seharîca tînin.
 
We preserve that rain, until it runs out. After it runs out,
we bring it with water tankers.

431
00:36:33,000 --> 00:36:36,000
Bîr qet tune, li gund bîr tune?
 
Are there no wells at all, no wells in the village?

432
00:36:36,000 --> 00:36:42,000
Bîr tune ne, bes seharîc hene. Seharîc ji kû têne em wê
mehefaza dikin. Ava baranê mehefaza dikin.
 
There are no wells, only water tanks. We preserve what comes
from the water tankers. We preserve the rainwater.

433
00:36:42,000 --> 00:36:45,000
Heta xelas bibe, xelas bû şûn da em seharîca tînin.
 
Until it runs out, after it runs out we bring water tankers.

434
00:36:45,000 --> 00:36:51,000
Û ji berî wê bi çend salan, wisa gundê me mezin e, sê hezar
neseme ye.
 
And a few years before that, our village is big like this,
it has three thousand people.

435
00:36:51,000 --> 00:36:56,000
Dorbê sê hezar kes li vî gundî zêdetir çêbûye.
 
There are around three thousand people in this village,
maybe more.

436
00:36:56,000 --> 00:37:03,000
Ji me re bîrek çêkirin, li ser esas yanî şebeke bide gund,
gundê me ra.
 
They made a well for us, basically to give a network to the
village, for our village.

437
00:37:03,000 --> 00:37:08,000
Gundê me, berê gundî me baladiye tê de çêbû ye, belde ye,
yanî bûye belde.
 
Our village, previously our village had a municipality in
it, it's a town, I mean it became a town.

438
00:37:08,000 --> 00:37:14,000
Bîrek kolan e, hukmet çêkiribû, hukmeta berê.
 
They dug a well, the government made it, the previous
government.

439
00:37:14,000 --> 00:37:23,000
Li alindara, wî darê binê alindara wî, bîr kolan e, av jê
derxistîye, naha ew bîre hîn neşixilîye.
 
At the Alindara, under that Alindara tree, a well was dug,
water was extracted from it, now that well hasn't been
operated yet.

440
00:37:23,000 --> 00:37:28,000
Ev noka bîrê em avê lê tînin, yê ehlî ye.
 
This well we are bringing water from right now, is a local
one.

441
00:37:28,000 --> 00:37:34,000
Ewa ser erdê ye, yanî nehe dehe metir kolan e, av pêta ye,
ev dor av e û em wê avê tînin vedixwin.
 
It's on the surface, I mean it's dug nine or ten meters, the
water is shallow, there is water around and we bring that
water and drink it.

442
00:37:34,000 --> 00:37:41,000
Gimar jî tê de heye, herî jî tê de heye, yanî tiştên ne sihî
tê de hene.
 
There is dirt in it, there is mud in it, I mean there are
unhygienic things in it.

443
00:37:41,000 --> 00:37:44,000
Welo kanî, qet tune li gund kanî?
 
Well, a spring, is there no spring at all in the village?

444
00:37:44,000 --> 00:37:48,000
Kanî sethî ne, mewsimî ne. Baran barî, kanî çêdibe.
 
The springs are shallow, they are seasonal. If it rains, a
spring appears.

445
00:37:48,000 --> 00:37:54,000
Baran nebarî, av disekine. Ew jî yên ser erdê ne, yanî.
 
If it doesn't rain, the water stops. Those are also on the
surface, I mean.

446
00:37:54,000 --> 00:37:58,000
Em kanin bêjin hûn zor û zehmetî gelek derbarê ava we de
dikişînin.
 
We can say that you are experiencing a lot of hardship and
difficulty regarding your water.

447
00:37:58,000 --> 00:38:05,000
Gelek pir e. Ev bîra cihê heza, rêxistin hene, alîkarî me
bikin, me re bişixulînin.
 
It's a lot. This well here, there are organizations, they
could help us, operate it for us.

448
00:38:05,000 --> 00:38:09,000
Bîr hazir e, bes mucered temdîd û defih, avê pê ve din.
 
The well is ready, just a simple extension and pumping,
supplying it with water.

449
00:38:09,000 --> 00:38:14,000
Û mimkine wê çaxê, melet alîkariya gundiyan bike, wê ra
harike.
 
And it's possible that then, the nation would help the
villagers, cooperate with them.

450
00:38:14,000 --> 00:38:21,000
Û em kanibin avê temîn kin. Em bi van tiştan pir av dikin,
yanî em bi destan dişixulin, bes îmkaniya me zeyîf e, yanî.
 
And we would be able to secure water. We do a lot for water
with these things, I mean we work with our hands, but our
capabilities are weak.

451
00:38:21,000 --> 00:38:31,000
Naha ta behsê xizmetguzarî kir, hejmara te got ku gundê wa
tu dibê gundewar, beladiye. Çi xizmet tê de hene?
 
Now you talked about services, you mentioned that your
village is a suburb, a municipality. What services are in
it?

452
00:38:31,000 --> 00:38:43,000
Dirêkê me tune ne, berî niha warê dirêkên kolanê şarihê em
tê de, dirtûz e em kî wek hev e.
 
We don't have roads, before now, regarding the streets and
the neighborhood we are in, it is unpaved, we are all the
same.

453
00:38:43,000 --> 00:38:48,000
Hasasî çêdike, pîsî, wekî hûn dibînin zift nekirine.
 
It causes allergies, dirt, as you can see, they haven't
paved it.

454
00:38:48,000 --> 00:38:48,000
Zift nekirin e, û noka jî ve zerfî jî, hukmeta berê ele xere
bû, ew ece ji, me hîn tiştî gundê ne dîtiye.
 
They haven't paved it?

455
00:38:48,000 --> 00:38:58,000
Zift nekirin e, û noka jî ve zerfî jî, hukmeta berê ele xere
bû, ew ece ji, me hîn tiştî gundê ne dîtiye.
 
They haven't paved it, and now in this situation too, the
previous government was ruined, so we haven't seen anything
for the village yet.

456
00:38:58,000 --> 00:39:05,000
Nizam çêke çênekir. Em dixwazin çêke, em dixwazin cîhetek me
tebenî ke me ra çêke.
 
The regime made it or didn't make it. We want it to be
built, we want a party to adopt us and build it for us.

457
00:39:05,000 --> 00:39:06,000
Ma qey ronî karebe?
 
What about electricity and lighting?

458
00:39:06,000 --> 00:39:18,000
Kahraba jî zehmet e. Karebe jî ji zû va me muhewela kir,
gava em muqabelek e bi mustesmîr ra çêkin li efrînê.
 
Electricity is also difficult. We tried for electricity a
long time ago, when we wanted to meet with an investor in
Afrin.

459
00:39:18,000 --> 00:39:27,000
Û şîmal heleb, karebe bi hal dikir. Em çûn, me ew kir, me mi
dîr tenfîzî ra.
 
And the North of Aleppo, they were managing the electricity.
We went, we did it, with the executive director.

460
00:39:27,000 --> 00:39:44,000
Ma muqabele badî sê meha, me kanî pê re rûniştin. Bi netîce
me ra go: Her muşterek...
 
We had an interview after three months, we were able to sit
down with him. As a result, he told us: Every subscriber...

461
00:39:44,000 --> 00:39:47,000
Her muşterek e bide we?
 
Every subscriber has to give to you?

462
00:39:47,000 --> 00:39:51,000
Duset û pêncî dolar ji me xwestin.
 
They asked for two hundred and fifty dollars from us.

463
00:39:51,000 --> 00:39:54,000
Û di cîyî duset û pêncî dolarî da...
 
And instead of two hundred and fifty dollars...

464
00:39:54,000 --> 00:39:55,000
Wa stiraş he ...
 
And the subscription...

465
00:39:55,000 --> 00:39:58,000
Hezar û pêncsed lîre yê sûriyê, iştîraka saetekê ye.
 
One thousand and five hundred Syrian pounds, is the
subscription for one hour.

466
00:39:58,000 --> 00:40:00,000
Iştîraka saetekê ye, erê.
 
The subscription for one hour, yes.

467
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:03,000
Sed kîlowat saetî em karabê didine gund.
 
We provide 100 kilowatt-hours of electricity to the village.

468
00:40:03,000 --> 00:40:11,000
Ê am hotin me ev meşrûa terh kirin nav gund, gotin:
"Îmkaniyat zeîf in, milê me nikarin bidin."
 
We came and proposed this project in the village, they said:
"Capabilities are weak, we can't afford it."

469
00:40:11,000 --> 00:40:12,000
Nikarin bidin...
 
They can't afford it...

470
00:40:12,000 --> 00:40:23,000
Sê kesî, çil kesî, got em ê bidin. Lê min li ser esas me got
em ê sed kesî temîn kin, sed kes tê da nebûn. Em niha ro ji
vê tiştî ne. Em niha nafikirin, em nakin.
 
Thirty people, forty people said we will pay. But on the
basis that we said we will secure 100 people, there weren't
100 people. We are now not doing this thing. We are not
thinking about it now, we are not doing it.

471
